I just tried out Moria (uMoria5.3.1) last week for the first time.  I
hadn't played Moria in four years, and I was pleasantly surprised.  It's
a pleasant change of pace from nethack, and I can see many really good
ideas that made me think "Well, now THAT makes more sense!"

Of course, Moria's got it's share of frustrating quirks, too, but I
guess you have to make sacrafices somewhere to make games playable.
Moria just made a lot of different decisions than NetHack.

If you haven't played Moria in a while, I'd recommend trying it out
(the NEW version...if you don't like Moria 1.0, you haven't really
been fair...  think how long Hack 1.0 would your interest if you tried
it now...)  I think playing Moria has rekindled much of my interest
in nethack, so I've been playing them BOTH more often.  Hmm...maybe
that's NOT such a good thing...

FTP available at kukulcan.berkeley.edu, I think, in something/wilson.
